title: The KPD launches a revolt!
subtitle: Is it time for a German Soviet?
new-page: true
view-if: revolution_progress >= 10
go-to: betrayal if in_popular_front = 1 or in_left_front = 1; opp_response if spd_in_government = 0; gov_response if spd_in_government = 1 and in_popular_front = 0 and in_left_front = 0
on-arrival: revolution_progress = 0
tags: event
max-visits: 4

= The October Revolt

Filled with revolutionary fervor, the KPD has mobilized the RFB and its supporters. A general strike has been declared and the RFB has been called to fight.

The situation is heating up, fast. Barricades are constructed, armed civilians patrol the streets, and isolated firefights have broken out across Berlin. We must do something about the situation.

@betrayal
on-arrival: z_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10; dvp_relation -= 15; lvp_relation -= 12; ddp_right += 3; dvp_right += 5; workers_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 10; old_middle_spd -= 10; rural_spd -= 5

The KPD has used its position in government to sabotage and infiltrate government institutions, weakening our potential responses. We, of course, receive the brunt of the blame-perhaps rightfully so.

- @join
- @beg
- @suppress
- @crush

@gov_response

Our position in government gives us advantages in dealing with this revolt, but could also prove a liability.

- @join
- @beg
- @suppress
- @crush

@opp_response

We are in the opposition; the revolt's fate rests with the current coalition. Still, we can issue a statement and deploy the Reichsbanner... if we want.

- @join

@join
title: Alle Macht den Arbeitern!
subtitle: Capitalism is buckling at the knees; the time for action is NOW!

We have issued a statement supporting the revolution, and have called for the Reichsbanner to fight alongside the KPD, much to the shock of our reformist elements and former coalition partners.

With our entrance into the conflict, things have started to swing in favor of the KPD. The Reichsbanner is paralyzed by indecision, as are our loyal police and soldiers.

- @left_civil_war

@beg
title: The KPD must listen to reason!
subtitle: We will plea with the KPD to cease this revolutionary madness.
go-to: beg_yay if kpd_relation > 50; beg_nay if kpd_relation < 50; beg_mid if kpd_relation = 50

We have dispatched several leftist SPD leaders including Toni Sender, Friedrich Stampfer, and Kurt Rosenfeld to personally plead to the KPD the weakness and fragility of their position.

@beg_yay

We argue that the KPD's move will only weaken the proletariat, pointing to the relative weakness of the RFB and KPD overall. We demand that they issue a statement calling for revolutionaries to lay down their arms.

Faced with this reality, the KPD reluctantly agrees - under a few conditions. First, the KPD and RFB must remain unbanned. Second, no action can be taken against any KPD members or their leaders.

- @accept
- @refuse

@accept
title: Very well, then.
subtitle: Another crisis averted. Peace it is!
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 10; dvp_relation -= 15; lvp_relation -= 15; workers_kpd -= 15; workers_spd += 5; new_middle_spd += 10; old_middle_spd += 5; rural_spd += 5; pacifism += 2

Reluctantly, the KPD has for the most part called off the general strike and ordered the RFB to lay down its arms. Resistance has largely stopped throughout the streets and across Germany.

This move has caused a great stir within the KPD, with many crying for a leadership change. However, the SPD has benefited greatly; it has received much of the credit for saving Germany from a bloody civil war.

@refuse
title: Outrageous!
subtitle: The KPD is in no position to make demands of us!
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 15

We refuse to accept these outrageous demands; thanks to the KPD, violence may be necessary after all.

- @suppress
- @crush

@beg_mid

We argue that the KPD's move will only weaken the proletariat, pointing to the relative weakness of the RFB and KPD overall. We demand that they issue a statement calling for revolutionaries to lay down their arms.

Unfortunately, the stubborn communists are blinded by the excitement of the revolution, and refuse to back down.

- @suppress
- @crush

@beg_nay
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 10

The KPD refuses to even hear us out, turning away our ambassadors with threats of violence and worse. At least we now know where they stand.

- @suppress
- @crush

@suppress
title: This revolt must be contained.
subtitle: Deploy the police and Reichsbanner to maintain order in the streets.
go-to: suppress_bam if kpd_relation > 50; suppress_shh if kpd_relation < 50; suppress_ehh if kpd_relation = 50

@suppress_bam
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 15; new_middle_spd -= 10

Despite our specific orders to maintain order and deescalate the streets, the reactionary police forces seem to have done everything they could have to escalate the situation instead. Berlin has become a warzone, as police fire at even innocent civilians.

The fledgling revolt has been crushed, but at what cost? Hundreds of innocent civilians have died and much of the city is destroyed. This will be difficult to recover from.

@suppress_shh
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 5; kpd_relation -= 15; soviet_relation -= 2; left_dissent += 15

The revolt has been successfully quelled by the Prussian police. Within a few days, fighting has mostly died down within the streets and many KPD leaders have been arrested.

@suppress_ehh
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 10; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 5; rural_spd -=5

The police are too weak and ineffective to contain the revolt; whether this is due to a lack of funding or kpd sabotage will remain unknown.

The Reichswehr under Groener has taken charge, deploying the Reichswehr into the street in order to "maintain order." All hell has broken loose.

- @left_civil_war

@crush
title: Unleash the Reichswehr!
subtitle: This opportunistic, Bolshevik revolt must be crushed before it gets out of control!
go-to: crush_yay if kpd_relation > 50; crush_nay if kpd_relation <= 50
on-arrival: z_relation += 15; ddp_relation += 10; dvp_relation += 15; workers_spd -= 20; new_middle_spd -= 10; old_middle_spd += 5

@crush_yay

The revolt has been totally crushed only a few days after its beginning. The streets are dominated by the Reichswehr, countless workers have died, and several prominent communist leaders have been murdered.

- @victory_mid

@victory_mid
title: Victory, but at what cost?
on-arrival: kpd_relation -= 50; workers_spd -= 5

The revolt has been destroyed, much to the approval of the bourgeois parties, but the KPD - and the workers they represent - will likely never forgive us.

Victory?

@crush_nay

It seems that the brutality of the Reichswehr has only strengthened the communists' resolve, and the RFB refuses to back down. Revolts are springing up all across Germany; the situation has gotten out of control.

- @left_civil_war
